MID_LGV_1_M06_Kai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Kai_m01_001: I figured out there's a training exercise you can only\ndo in the city! Dodging through the crowds!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Kai_m01_002: At first, I had to keep stopping because I was nearly\nbumping into people. But I got the hang of it.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Kai_m01_003: Now, I'm getting really good at avoiding people,\nand I'm able to do it faster than ever!
MID_LGA_1_M06_Kai_m01: <BLN>I'm getting really good!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Bel_m01_001: I have to ask Gabriel to bring me a new wooden\ndummy.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Bel_m01_002: This'll be...oh, probably the two hundredth or so I've\ngone through. I wear them out quickly.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Bel_m01_003: But what choice do I have? I have to keep training if\nI want to keep winning.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Bel_m01: <BLN>You can never do enough.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Dit_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Dit_m01_001: The gods of this land... They dwell here, speaking\nand acting as we do. They feel as we feel.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Dit_m01_002: They interest me much more than the vague tales we\nare told in Fódlan.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Dit_m01: <BLN>There are gods of many stripes.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tal_m01_001: Dinners are great for people watching. Not even gods\ncan hide their true natures with their mouths full.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tal_m01_002: Watch closely, and there's a good chance you'll see a\nside of them you didn't expect... A side you can use.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tal_m01_003: Even if they try to hide themselves, that only makes\nit more obvious. Hah. You should try it sometime.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Tal_m01: <BLN>Ever tried people watching?
MID_LGV_1_M06_Orh_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Orh_m02_001: Life in the imperial capital seems to revolve around\nliving closely together with many others.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Orh_m02_002: I've become friends with people I meet every\nmorning at the water station.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Orh_m02_003: I can easily carry 10 buckets of water at once, so\nthey've come to call me "mighty kitty"!
MID_LGA_1_M06_Orh_m02: <BLN>I'm making friends!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Orh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Orh_m01_001: Credna asked me to never reveal my face in front\nof people here. I've failed him on such a grand scale.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Orh_m01_002: Oh! And my wonderful mask was ruined! It was\nmade so carefully by hand too...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Orh_m01_003: There must be a way I can get that irresponsible\nknight to pay for the repair.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Orh_m01: <BLN>The people of the capital...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Seo_m01_001: The people of Saramis are dauntless warriors, but we\nare not crude. Many in the empire fail to grasp this.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Seo_m01_002: There are even those who consider us intellectually\ninferior because we eschew the written word.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Seo_m01_003: I detest this misconception. In my darker moments,\nI feel inclined to beat the intolerance out of them.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Seo_m01_004: <NCA>Encourage her.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Seo_m01_005: <NCB>Discourage her.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Seo_m01_006: I mustn't. As queen of Saramis, I cannot be seen to\nstrike the people of the empire. Gah!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Seo_m01_007: Doing so would only tarnish my reputation further.\nThank you for helping me see reason.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Seo_m01: <BLN>It is difficult to restrain myself.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Led_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Led_m01_001: Eugh! Snakes and frogs are so revolting.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Led_m01_002: Kalla once told me that there are distant lands where\npeople can control snakes with flutes.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Led_m01_003: The thought of it makes my skin crawl.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Led_m01: <BLN>Disgusting...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Anh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Anh_m01_001: Some of the gods have very strange interests.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Anh_m01_002: I heard that Smyrnos, the Spell-Scholar, enlarged\na cat to act as his servant.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Anh_m01_003: I don't know if it was an experiment or if he did it\nto amuse himself. It's hard to believe either way.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Anh_m01: <BLN>It's hard to believe.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tia_m01_001: Cai doesn't want to do anything lately except fish.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tia_m01_002: I admit I can't swim, so I'm afraid of even being close\nto water. But I still want to have fun with him.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tia_m01_003: <NCA>Suggest she find something they both like.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tia_m01_004: <NCB>Tell her to learn to swim.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tia_m01_005: <ACA>That's a good idea! I'll look into it and see if I can't\nfind something else we could do.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tia_m01_006: <ACA>A wonderful suggestion, Your Majesty! I'll look into it\nand see if I can't find something else we could do.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tia_m01_007: <ACB>I suppose all it takes is practice, right? It's a bit\nfrightening though...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tia_m01_008: <ACB>I suppose all it takes is practice, right? It's a bit\nfrightening though...
MID_LGA_1_M06_Tia_m01: <BLN>What to do...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Pet_m01_001: I look up to men who are brave and strong.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Pet_m01_002: I wonder if I'll grow up to be as strong as some of\nthe fighters here?
MID_LGA_1_M06_Pet_m01: <BLN>I look up to them...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Hur_m01_001: All the vulkans are strong, sure. But they all have\ntells when fighting.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Hur_m01_002: It's not hard with most of them, but I still haven't\nbeen able to beat Centurio. Not even once.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Hur_m01_003: He's faster than me, stronger than me...but one of\nthese days I'm going to get the better of him.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Hur_m01: <BLN>I'll beat him someday...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Max_m01_001: Heh heh HEH! I'm gonna be laughing about that\nfight with the wing soldier for a long time.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Max_m01_002: And I mean, the commissioner, Poloni—his\nfavoritism is so depraved, even I'm shocked.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Max_m01_003: They claim this is some religious thing to bring back\nthe Divine Emperor, but clearly it's all a farce.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Max_m01: <BLN>It makes me laugh!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gol_m01_001: I always thought, the more muscles you've got,\nthe better.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gol_m01_002: I mean, there's so much you can do if you're strong!\nYou can break stuff, you can fend off attacks...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gol_m01_003: Only, the harder I trained, the more people got\nscared of me. At least now I'm used to it.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gol_m01_004: <NCA>Tell him some accept him for who he is.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gol_m01_005: <NCB>Ask if he's tried losing muscle.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gol_m01_006: <ACA>You know what? You're right! My brother's not\nscared of me. Thanks for cheering me up!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gol_m01_007: <ACB>Huh? Nah, I can't do that. Then I'd get weak.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Gol_m01: <BLN>Stronger's not always better.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gat_m01_001: Many seem to fear the White-Maned Demon. I think\nthey simply misunderstand his nature.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gat_m01_002: To me, there's no man who's more pleasant and\nenjoyable to talk to.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gat_m01_003: But perhaps that's something you could only learn by\nfighting alongside him.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Gat_m01: <BLN>They're wrong about him.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Dan_m01_001: Coffee—I need coffee. I was up all night, and now I\nrequire an elixir dark and thick as hell fog.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Dan_m01_002: Pair that with a meal I can eat with one hand,\nand the writing will flow.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Dan_m01_003: Yes. I'll go and procure them from the market,\nand then... Then I can stay up one more night!
MID_LGA_1_M06_Dan_m01: <BLN>I need it. Now.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Fab_m01_001: To think that such a high-ranking member of the\nChurch of Seiros has come to Dagda.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Fab_m01_002: It seems that he, too, is concealing his identity, so our\naims are best served by avoiding contact.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Fab_m01_003: No matter where I roam in this land, trouble nips at\nmy heels. I must be cautious.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Fab_m01: <BLN>This Seteth individual...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Esm_m01_001: *sigh* Some days you just can't win. Am I to blame?
MID_LGV_1_M06_Esm_m01_002: I was walking down a busy street when a carriage\nlost its wheel and the whole thing tipped over.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Esm_m01_003: Everyone was just standing around, so I lifted it up.\nTHEN they started panicking!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Esm_m01_004: <NCA>Point out that some people must be grateful.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Esm_m01_005: <NCB>Suggest it is better to blend in.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Esm_m01_006: <ACA>You think so? Maybe you're right. I hope so,\nanyway! Thanks.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Esm_m01_007: <ACB>Why, though? If I'm strong enough to help, I should\nhelp. Why do I need to hide it?
MID_LGA_1_M06_Esm_m01: <BLN>I was only trying to help...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Urs_m01_001: Most people believe Talimun is this complicated\nmystery. But the key to understanding him is simple.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Urs_m01_002: If you can set your expectations aside, you're able to\nsee his actions with a kind of bird's-eye view.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Urs_m01_003: Then again, he still manages to surprise me with\nmesses that border on lunacy...
MID_LGA_1_M06_Urs_m01: <BLN>Just a thought.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sim_m01_001: Hm. So, in the Heroic Games, they choose battles\nfrom history and have the fighters reenact them.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sim_m01_002: Must be to entertain the audience. Or maybe to help\nstir up some fighter instinct? Heh. I don't know.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sim_m01_003: I get it, the audience wants a spectacle. But nothing\nbeats the real thing.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Sim_m01: <BLN>It's so pointless.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lou_m01_001: You wouldn't believe how expensive Talimun's\njewelry is!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lou_m01_002: If a normal person sold just one piece, they'd be set\nfor at least a year.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lou_m01_003: How many years could someone last if they sold all of\nit? That he just wears it around makes my head spin.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Lou_m01: <BLN>He just wears it like it's nothing.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Fia_m01_001: I enjoy spicy foods, especially the ones that make\nyou feel warm inside.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Fia_m01_002: But whenever I add spices to my meals, I tend to get\nthe strangest looks...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Fia_m01_003: So I only use them when I'm with friends.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Fia_m01: <BLN>Strange...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Die_m01_001: I should be doing everything I can so Orchel can\nfocus on winning her matches.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Die_m01_002: But to do that, I should always take care of the\ndamn foes coming her way too...
MID_LGA_1_M06_Die_m01: <BLN>Come on...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lor_m01_001: I must be doing fine with my temple duties. Father\nNomved shared some Dagsion sweets with me.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lor_m01_002: The sweets in this city are SO sweet. I love them!\nI'd eat 'em every day if I could.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lor_m01_003: I bet the priest lady would make them for me. But\nnah, I shouldn't bug her with silly things like that.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Lor_m01: <BLN>They're SO good!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Set_m01_001: I never expected to see a Hero's Relic here on the\nDagdan continent.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Set_m01_002: It's far from ideal, but in another way, it's fortunate\nthat I encountered him here.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Set_m01_003: Had I not, it's possible that a disaster could have\noccurred here, outside the Church's purview.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Set_m01: <BLN>Perhaps it was meant to be.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Nin_m01_001: I agree... Yes, thank you... I knew it already...\nBut yes, I appreciate it...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Nin_m01_002: Powerful emotions swell at the games... Malicious\nmotivations creep in the shadows...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Nin_m01_003: Yes, rest assured... If they cross Father and the\nothers, I will kill them... All will be well...
MID_LGA_1_M06_Nin_m01: <BLN>Alright... I understand...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Bon_m01_001: Dagsion is home to certain temptations I have had\nto take pains to avoid.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Bon_m01_002: There is writing everywhere—on signs, placards,\nand so forth. It would be unthinkable in Saramis.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Bon_m01_003: I must take care, lest they entice my gaze. Her\nMajesty would be most displeased with me...
MID_LGA_1_M06_Bon_m01: <BLN>I must be vigilant.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tob_m01_001: Man, I'm hungry. Maybe I'll go grab some more dried\nmeat from the provisions.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tob_m01_002: Or I could go hunting and eat in the wild. It's fun to\nsplit firewood and cook over the fire.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Tob_m01_003: It's a tough call. The kinda thing that's best pondered\nover a mug of ale!
MID_LGA_1_M06_Tob_m01: <BLN>Man, I'm hungry.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lil_m01_001: I know the forests of Saramis pretty well, so it's been\nfun to explore some unfamiliar woods for a change.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lil_m01_002: The trees smell different, and they've got different\nanimals living in 'em. Everything's new and fresh.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lil_m01_003: I oughta make some time to go hunting when I'm\nnext off work.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Lil_m01: <BLN>I like the novelty.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lys_m01_001: For an event hosted by the temple, unfairness seems\nrampant in the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lys_m01_002: I thought the matches would be clean, but there have\nbeen some rather underhanded combatants.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Lys_m01: <BLN>How reprehensible.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Buc_m01_001: The temple soldiers guard the capital, even at night.\nIt's likely much safer here than beyond the city.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Buc_m01_002: Not to say that it's without its dangers...as I should\nprobably remind milady.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Buc_m01_003: I heard that there was a strange man wailing in\nthe tavern. Who knows who he was?
MID_LGV_1_M06_Buc_m01_004: <NCA>Tell him you'll keep him informed.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Buc_m01_005: <NCB>Ask if this wailing man was him.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Buc_m01_006: <ACA>I appreciate that. The more information we\nexchange, the more easily we'll evade danger.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Buc_m01_007: <ACA>I appreciate that. The more information we\nexchange, the more easily we will evade danger.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Buc_m01_008: <ACB>Is that meant to be a joke? I like a drink now and\nagain. I do not disgrace myself in public.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Buc_m01_009: <ACB>No... I like a drink now and again, but I will not\ndisgrace myself in public.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Buc_m01: <BLN>I must be sure to tell milady.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sci_m01_001: Ahh, the joys of a good drink! Especially when it's\nshared with a beautiful woman.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sci_m01_002: Though of course, I would never do anything so\ndisgusting as use alcohol to entice someone.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sci_m01_003: I use the language of love to woo my paramours.\nDrink is a treat, never an inducement.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Sci_m01: <BLN>Nice as it may be...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Moo_m01_001: I saw a guy earlier who seemed really happy...\nor had been drinking, maybe.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Moo_m01_002: It's no fun taking care of drunk people, but it can be\nkind of a kick watching them.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Moo_m01: <BLN>At least he was having fun?
MID_LGV_1_M06_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Mic_m01_001: A while ago I ran into Guzran. He was mouthing off\nabout some promising young fighter he'd discovered.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Mic_m01_002: Before long, he had moved on to boasting about\nhow he taught them everything they know.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Mic_m01_003: Same old song and dance. The man never changes.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Mic_m01: <BLN>He never changes.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Oly_m01_001: Earlier, as I was taking an early-morning stroll, I saw\nNezha training on his own.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Oly_m01_002: He'd always struck me as rather a rough fellow!\nIt was touching to see him put that effort in.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Oly_m01_003: One is reminded that focused effort can be a\nbeautiful, valuable thing.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Oly_m01: <BLN>It was striking!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Naz_m01_001: Sometimes, it feels weird that everyone goes to\nrestaurants at mealtimes.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Naz_m01_002: Back in the village, food was more scarce. People ate\nwhen they could.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Naz_m01_003: If you're hungry, you fill your belly. No matter what\ntime it is.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Naz_m01: <BLN>Is it weird?
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sar_m01_001: It's not surprising that the Heroic Games can be a\nbit unfair at times.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sar_m01_002: It's an event sponsored by the temples, after all.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Sar_m01: <BLN>It's not surprising.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Dai_m01_001: Anatolia talks about how we should use Salamanders\ncarefully, and only when it's absolutely critical.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Dai_m01_002: Not that she, or anyone else, is super careful. They're\nall so rough with their gear that it's hard to watch.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Dai_m01_003: I do maintenance on them, so they'll keep working.\nBut I wish everybody would be a bit more careful.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Dai_m01: <BLN>They're all so rough on their gear.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Hal_m01_001: We've been meeting important people lately.\nI never imagined doing anything like this!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Hal_m01_002: I think I've managed not to embarrass myself so far.\nMy parents raised me well!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Hal_m01_003: Thanks, Dad. Thanks, Mom!
MID_LGA_1_M06_Hal_m01: <BLN>My parents raised me well.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Guj_m01_001: I'm kind of popular with the ladies. It's always been\nthat way. So many epic evenings!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Guj_m01_002: I could never pin my heart on any one of them.\nThat would just be unfair to all the rest!
MID_LGA_1_M06_Guj_m01: <BLN>I just couldn't do it.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Yan_m01_001: So Alexandra developed her talents working as a\nknight of Jurah's temple, did she?
MID_LGV_1_M06_Yan_m01_002: She, like me, has struggled to stay on a true and\nrighteous path, pulled at by other influences.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Yan_m01_003: And still, what unwavering commitment she has for\nher personal faith. Almost inconceivable to me.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Yan_m01: <BLN>Intriguing...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Iio_m01_001: It was a bitter experience, casting aside my status\nas a knight. But I'm glad I became a mercenary.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Iio_m01_002: I've been able to visit many places, meet a lot of\npeople, and learn about different walks of life.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Iio_m01_003: By that, I came to my own true calling—seeking a\nlord with great ideals to serve.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Iio_m01: <BLN>My path is clear.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Pep_m01_001: We ourselves have tried to experience a tavern. But\nwe were banished, told it was no place for "kids."
MID_LGV_1_M06_Pep_m01_002: What impertinence! We wanted only to see what the\nembottled merrymaking of Dagsion was like!
MID_LGA_1_M06_Pep_m01: <BLN>What impertinence!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Noc_m01_001: Watching the Heroic Games has made me itch to\nget back to training.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Noc_m01_002: Not that I stop watching right then and there to\ntrain, but I train for longer when I do it.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Noc_m01_003: Anyway, my arms are just going to get stronger\nand stronger!
MID_LGA_1_M06_Noc_m01: <BLN>It's hard to be so still.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sop_m01_001: When I'm out in the city, I often get called the\nGrumbling Tummy by this little kid.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sop_m01_002: Is my stomach grumbling that often? I'm usually\non the hunt for a snack, but I'm not always hungry!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Sop_m01_003: Then again, I don't remember the last time I wasn't\nlooking for a snack. Maybe I should embrace it...
MID_LGA_1_M06_Sop_m01: <BLN>Isn't it rude?
MID_LGV_1_M06_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Cat_m01_001: The number of cheats and swindlers is growing\namong those selling things at the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Cat_m01_002: I don't miss much, however, so I won't be fooled.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Cat_m01_003: Furthermore, I carry little money with me, so there's\nnot much to be gained from trying.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Cat_m01: <BLN>Not a problem for me.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Ned_m01_001: Once again...I got myself surrounded by soldiers I\nknew long ago, when we were all friends.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Ned_m01_002: They wouldn't stop asking me to tell them stories of\nmy travels—or to show them my battle moves.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Ned_m01_003: It's not bad, really. Just awkward when former\nfriends are now treating me so differently.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Ned_m01: <BLN>It happened again...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Zac_m01_001: What pretty ladies there are around these parts!\nTroves and troves of 'em!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Zac_m01_002: But it's tough being a bandit lookin' for love! They\ndon't want this life. Huh, just takes gettin' used to!
MID_LGA_1_M06_Zac_m01: <BLN>Pretty, pretty!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Maj_m01_001: Dagsion's prison cells are rock solid. Never could\nbreak out. I tried though!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Maj_m01_002: Must've had them made tough specially for me!
MID_LGA_1_M06_Maj_m01: <BLN>Tried my best!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Ven_m01_001: Bunch of li'l squirts! Why'd I ever say I'd play in their\nsilly soldier games!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Ven_m01_002: I treated them all seriously, like tiny recruits. They\nran circles around me, caterwauling in delight!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Ven_m01_003: And the parents—atrocious! They said they hoped I\nhad...fun. Where was the gratitude for my service?!
MID_LGA_1_M06_Ven_m01: <BLN>Never again!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Jas_m01_001: Hmm, what to do... Someone recommended some\nnew defensive equipment to me.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Jas_m01_002: And it's good, for sure, but at that price? There's\nnothing wrong with what I'm using now.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Jas_m01_003: Ah, I'll sleep on it and make my decision tomorrow.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Jas_m01: <BLN>What to do...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Ale_m01_001: It's fun to look down at the city from a lofty position.\nI've discovered so many things that way.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Ale_m01_002: For instance, I saw Lysander staring upward—at\nthe sky, his mind sort of adrift.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Ale_m01_003: I waved at him, but he didn't notice. That's pretty\nodd, given he's usually such a sharp person.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Ale_m01: <BLN>When I'm on Bucephalus...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Cen_m01_001: I expect today to be another one full of trouble. My\nsubordinates bring me something new every day.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Cen_m01_002: It's proof everyone's working diligently, but it also\nmeans there's more trouble than we're used to.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Cen_m01: <BLN>Another day of reports...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Kir_m01_001: The naval battle in the qualifiers was a stunner!\nPeople are talking about it in the taverns.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Kir_m01_002: When I hear about it, I miss the days of wreaking\nhavoc out on the open sea.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Kir_m01_003: Mark my words—I'll get my pirate crew back\ntogether and spread terror on the Danann Sea again!
MID_LGA_1_M06_Kir_m01: <BLN>I miss the sea.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gab_m01_001: Vandahl Trading is the long-running, proven outfit,\nwhile Mandalan's more of a newcomer.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gab_m01_002: If you're doing business in Dagsion, you can't avoid\neither of 'em, but... I don't know.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Gab_m01_003: I don't much like dealing with the Mandalan folks.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Gab_m01: <BLN>Between the two...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lin_m01_001: The only visitors I used to get were people who knew\nto fear me.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lin_m01_002: But I don't understand my latest crop of visitors\nat all.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Lin_m01_003: Maybe there's no one left on the surface who even\nremembers me anymore.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Lin_m01: <BLN>A strange bunch of visitors...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Nat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Nat_m01_001: So! This is Dagsion, huh? Impressive.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Nat_m01_002: It's so much larger than Grand Aragon,\nthe royal capital.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Nat_m01_003: But I guess that's what you'd expect from the seat of\npower in the Dagdan Empire.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Nat_m01: <BLN>The imperial capital!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Hri_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Hri_m01_001: Quite a lively place! I like it.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Hri_m01_002: The chancellor must be plotting something if she\nsummoned us here so quickly...
MID_LGV_1_M06_Hri_m01_003: But at least we get to do a little sightseeing.
MID_LGA_1_M06_Hri_m01: <BLN>It's so lively.
MID_LGV_1_M06_Miw_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_Miw_m01_001: You mustn't go near the painting! Never!
MID_LGV_1_M06_Miw_m01_002: You risk falling under the glare of a fearsome eye!\nI'm begging you...
MID_LGA_1_M06_Miw_m01: <BLN>Don't go near it!
MID_LGV_1_M06_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B01_m01_001: Do they really not sell fresh pegasus cheese anywhere\nhere in Dagsion?
MID_LGV_1_M06_B01_m01_002: I haven't found it in the marketplace, but I'm\ndesperate to taste that gentle sweetness for myself!
MID_LGA_1_M06_B01_m01: <BLN>No vendor seems to sell it...
MID_LGV_1_M06_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B02_m01_001: I was really rooting for the Silver Knights of Tellus.\nThat Alexandra's a cutie.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B02_m01_002: She must have more time on her hands since she\nlost. Maybe she has some time for me, heehee.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B02_m01: <BLN>It's a shame she lost...
MID_LGV_1_M06_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B03_m01_001: I came all the way from my nomadic clan in Almyra\nto see the fierce battles of the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B03_m01_002: It's interesting to see Dagda's orderly system of\ngovernment, managed by the temples.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B03_m01_003: Where I'm from, we have more freedom but less\nsolidarity.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B03_m01: <BLN>My homeland is very different.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B04_m01_001: I finally crafted a pair of spectacles that my master\napproves of! It's taken so long to get to this point.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B04_m01_002: I hope they find a home once they go on sale. I think\nthey will—I gave them a very cute design.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B04_m01: <BLN>I finally did it!
MID_LGV_1_M06_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B05_m01_001: Was that the Lady of Lilies seated next to the Divine\nSovereign in the luxury seats?
MID_LGV_1_M06_B05_m01_002: Lord Solel was famed for his devotion to his late\nwife. I'm surprised he's taken up with a mistress.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B05_m01: <BLN>Is that what's going on?
MID_LGV_1_M06_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B06_m01_001: A friend invited me to work with him at a main\ntemple, but I prefer to stay at the branch temple.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B06_m01_002: After all, Dagsion is the greatest city in all the land.\nWho would ever want to leave?!
MID_LGV_1_M06_B06_m01_003: Though maybe I should be keeping that opinion\nto myself...
MID_LGA_1_M06_B06_m01: <BLN>It might be improper of me, but...
MID_LGV_1_M06_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B07_m01_001: Credna's temple is a nice place. They provide work\nfor plenty of laborers and cargo haulers like me.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B07_m01_002: There's plenty to do, from hauling ore and bitumen\nto taking a turn working the bellows.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B07_m01_003: Plenty of interesting folk to meet too, with all the\nartisans coming and going. I like it.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B07_m01: <BLN>It's a nice place.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B08_m01_001: I'm actually glad Alexandra lost. She could stand to\nbe taken down a peg, if you ask me.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B08_m01_002: She didn't know how to use that Arc she got a hold\nof—typical privileged brat. Makes my blood boil.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B08_m01: <BLN>Serves her right!
MID_LGV_1_M06_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B09_m01_001: I wanna drive a carriage when I'm older. That seat\nlooks so fun to sit in!
MID_LGV_1_M06_B09_m01_002: If only I could get my hands on some reins and start\npracticing...but I don't know anybody who has some.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B09_m01: <BLN>It looks so fun...
MID_LGV_1_M06_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B10_m01_001: I'm as hungry as I am broke. Maybe the temples can\nspare some food for me.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B10_m01_002: Would it help if I prayed harder? Could I squeeze\nsome money, clothes, and shelter from them too?
MID_LGA_1_M06_B10_m01: <BLN>I'll do anything...
MID_LGV_1_M06_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B12_m01_001: My stint in the Heroic Games is over. Better start\nlooking for a new meal ticket.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B12_m01_002: Maybe Kashgar or somewhere. Gotta be plenty of\nwork for a mercenary in a land of barbarians.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B12_m01: <BLN>Where to next?
MID_LGV_1_M06_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B13_m01_001: I'm going to get to the magic metropolis across the\nsea, no matter what it takes!
MID_LGV_1_M06_B13_m01_002: There must be some company or other willing to\noffer passage on a trading ship.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B13_m01: <BLN>It's my dream!
MID_LGV_1_M06_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B14_m01_001: The usual way to transport goods is by land or sea.\nBut the sky might be an option too.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B14_m01_002: I'd get it delivered in no time at all on bau-back!\nThough I'd have to turn down any oversize cargo.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B14_m01: <BLN>Any work for me?
MID_LGV_1_M06_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B15_m01_001: The Vandahl Trading Company's got its fingers in\nevery pie. Wherever you go, people know the name.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B15_m01_002: I can't compete with an outfit like that. Better to\ncarve out my own niche.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B15_m01: <BLN>For scale, they can't be beat.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B16_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B16_m01_001: We're headed for Megaira, royal capital of Saramis,\nbut there are lots of special preparations first.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B16_m01_002: Since the written word is taboo there, contracts and\nsignatures will get you nowhere.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B16_m01_003: Instead, they exchange pictorial details of any\ntransaction. Which means I need to hire an artist.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B16_m01: <BLN>This calls for special preparations.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B17_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B17_m01_001: Queen Aswan has been in good spirits ever since she\ncame to Dagsion.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B17_m01_002: Back home, she was in such low spirits that she\nwould often decline to eat.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B17_m01_003: Does she really love gladiatorial combat that much?\nHer and the Lady of Lilies... I just don't get nobles.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B17_m01: <BLN>They scare me a little.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B18_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B18_m01_001: I ended up training in magic under Smyrnos.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B18_m01_002: I thought it was an honor, but my father keeps\npushing me to try to become his consort.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B18_m01_003: He's got some nerve to even suggest such a thing.\nI'm there as a student, not a harlot! 
MID_LGA_1_M06_B18_m01: <BLN>The cheek of that man!
MID_LGV_1_M06_B19_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B19_m01_001: My son is getting married soon. It feels like just\nyesterday that he was born.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B19_m01_002: Has it been so long since the Saga of Aeneus inspired\nme to woo the woman who would become my wife?
MID_LGA_1_M06_B19_m01: <BLN>I feel the passage of time...
MID_LGV_1_M06_B20_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B20_m01_001: I came to see the famous painting of paradise on\nthe wall of this temple.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B20_m01_002: It's a very striking image... This on its own would\nhave been worth the trip.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B20_m01: <BLN>Truly incredible!
MID_LGV_1_M06_B21_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B21_m01_001: I've become smitten with Queen Theodora as I watch\nher progress through the games.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B21_m01_002: Ahh... Such untamed beauty...
MID_LGV_1_M06_B21_m01_003: Wh— It's you! Queen Theodora, in the flesh!\nThis is so embarrassing...
MID_LGA_1_M06_B21_m01: <BLN>She's like a goddess in battle!
MID_LGV_1_M06_B22_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B22_m01_001: I'm told that trading with Saramis is a real pain for\nmerchants since writing is forbidden there.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B22_m01_002: Apparently they pass down all their history and\nknowledge orally.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B22_m01_003: It says something about their stubbornness that they\nuphold Yu Phas's prohibition to this day.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B22_m01: <BLN>Why are they so difficult?
MID_LGV_1_M06_B23_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B23_m01_001: I thought I'd take my son to the training grounds,\nbut he didn't seem keen on the idea.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B23_m01_002: When I asked him why, he said he was afraid of the\ntraining dummies. That's kids for you.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B23_m01: <BLN>It's cute, in a way.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B24_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B24_m01_001: I hear that most folks in Saramis worship Yu Phas.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B24_m01_002: How dreadful. Why would they choose to revere the\nKeeper of Death and Night?
MID_LGA_1_M06_B24_m01: <BLN>It's just not normal!
MID_LGV_1_M06_B25_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B25_m01_001: There are a great many fighters worth watching in\nthe Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B25_m01_002: But if you can only follow one, I highly recommend\nthe Mystery Bride!
MID_LGA_1_M06_B25_m01: <BLN>She's one to watch...
MID_LGV_1_M06_B26_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B26_m01_001: The huge gulf to the southeast of Dagda is called the\nDanann Sea.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B26_m01_002: There's always a current flowing sunwise. A savvy\nsailor can make good use of it.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B26_m01_003: But it's rampant with pirates, so only the very brave\nsail those waters.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B26_m01_004: Myself, I prefer not to be boarded, so I steer clear.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B26_m01: <BLN>The Danann Sea is southeast.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B27_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B27_m01_001: Taking up a class can make it easier to develop\nparticular abilities.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B27_m01_002: For example, if you make a gladiator out of a weaker\ncombatant and let them keep at it...
MID_LGV_1_M06_B27_m01_003: they may find it easier than normal to build up\nstrength.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B27_m01_004: This effect is especially pronounced among the\nadvanced classes.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B27_m01_005: So ask yourself, do you want to enhance an ally's\nstrengths or shore up their weak points?
MID_LGA_1_M06_B27_m01: <BLN>Classes can work wonders.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B28_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B28_m01_001: The pirate Drake amassed magical artifacts that\nheld awesome power.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B28_m01_002: After his death, they were scattered far and wide\nacross the land.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B28_m01_003: Yet despite that, to this day we still know them as\nDrake's treasures.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B28_m01: <BLN>Ah, Drake's treasures...
MID_LGV_1_M06_B29_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B29_m01_001: Few in the empire's history have been honored with\nthe title of Flame Lord.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B29_m01_002: Those elevated to that position have statues erected\nin their honor, and their names sung in praise.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B29_m01_003: Explore Dagsion enough and you're bound to find\ntheir likenesses inscribed with their exploits.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B29_m01: <BLN>It's a prestigious title.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B30_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B30_m01_001: As the name suggests, the Gates of the Gods are\nportals intended for the divine.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B30_m01_002: By using the gods' pathways, one can travel in an\ninstant to a god's main temple.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B30_m01_003: But only the gods themselves, and a select few they\ndeem worthy, are permitted to use them.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B30_m01: <BLN>They are the pathways of the gods.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B31_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B31_m01_001: Long before Saramis was founded, there was a\nnation called Damascar in the south.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B31_m01_002: If it still stood today, it would be an even older\nkingdom than Arago.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B31_m01_003: Formed under the care of the goddess Yu Phas,\nDamascar had ties to the People of the White Egg.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B31_m01_004: But one day they incurred the wrath of Dagda the\nGreat and were annihilated utterly.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B31_m01_005: The Divine Emperor cast the blame on Yu Phas\nherself and put her to death for it.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B31_m01: <BLN>Let me tell you of Damascar...
MID_LGV_1_M06_B32_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B32_m01_001: Aurora was born from the union of Lord Solel\nand Yu Phas.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B32_m01_002: Regrettably, I have been unable to look upon her\nexalted face thus far.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B32_m01_003: They say she is beautiful to behold...assuming she\nactually exists.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B32_m01: <BLN>Aurora is a mystery.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B33_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B33_m01_001: Among the libraries in each god's temple are many\nbooks containing fantastical knowledge.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B33_m01_002: Yet it is strictly forbidden to remove or distribute\nknowledge or divine artifacts from the temples.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B33_m01_003: Even if one is allowed to peruse such a collection,\ncopying the information there is out of the question.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B33_m01_004: Anyone tempted to do such a thing should know that\nthe punishment is grave indeed.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B33_m01: <BLN>Knowledge is a treasure.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B34_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B34_m01_001: This is private property, and you're trespassing.\nSo scram.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B34_m01: <BLN>Nothing to see here.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B35_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M06_B35_m01_001: Do you know where the best view in Dagsion is?
MID_LGV_1_M06_B35_m01_002: Why, it's Dagda's temple! The place may as well\nhave been built in the heavens.
MID_LGV_1_M06_B35_m01_003: From there, one can look down on all of Dagsion.
MID_LGA_1_M06_B35_m01: <BLN>One view surpasses all the rest.